#
# Counter-example for gmeow:GateFatalUpsetShape: a gmeow:Finding on the principal
# gate-fatal up-set ↑(gmeow:severityError, gmeow:blockingBlocking,
# gmeow:standpointBinding) that is MISSING the derived verdict
# gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal. The shape's sh:sparql constraint fires
# because the up-set antecedent holds but the fatal verdict is absent, so
# validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (and no other finding —
# findingSeverity/findingCode/findingMessage satisfy gmeow:FindingShape, so the
# up-set shape is the sole violator). This proves the shape discriminates the
# up-set boundary (non-vacuous). Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl
# (ex:ecGateFatalMissing). Lives under tests/ (NOT examples/) so the global
# make validate gate does not reject it.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/diagnostics/tests/> .

ex:fFatalMissing
    a gmeow:Finding ;
    gmeow:findingSeverity gmeow:severityError ;
    gmeow:findingStandpoint gmeow:standpointBinding ;
    gmeow:findingCategory logic:FindingContradictionWitness ;
    gmeow:findingCode "reason.contradiction" ;
    gmeow:findingMessage "a forbidden contradiction witness on the gate-fatal up-set, missing its derived fatal verdict" .
